public inherited sharing class ErpCustomerSync implements Queueable, Database.AllowsCallouts {

    private static final Integer MAX_BATCH_SIZE = 200;
    private final List<CustomerPayload> payloads;

    public class CustomerPayload {
        public String salesforceId;
        public String name;
        public String country;

        public CustomerPayload(Account acc) {
            this.salesforceId = String.valueOf(acc.Id);
            this.name = acc.Name;
            this.country = String.isBlank(acc.BillingCountry) ? null : acc.BillingCountry;
        }
    }

    public ErpCustomerSync(List<CustomerPayload> payloads) {
        this.payloads = payloads;
    }

    public static void enqueueSync(List<Account> newAccounts) {
        if (newAccounts == null || newAccounts.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        List<CustomerPayload> currentBatch = new List<CustomerPayload>();

        for (Account acc : newAccounts) {
            currentBatch.add(new CustomerPayload(acc));

            if (currentBatch.size() == MAX_BATCH_SIZE) {
                enqueueJobIfAllowed(currentBatch);
                currentBatch = new List<CustomerPayload>();
            }
        }

        if (!currentBatch.isEmpty()) {
            enqueueJobIfAllowed(currentBatch);
        }
    }

    private static void enqueueJobIfAllowed(List<CustomerPayload> batchToSync) {
        if (Limits.getQueueableJobs() < Limits.getLimitQueueableJobs()) {
            System.enqueueJob(new ErpCustomerSync(batchToSync));
        }
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (this.payloads == null || this.payloads.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
        req.setEndpoint('callout:ERP/api/customers');
        req.setMethod('POST');
        req.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
        req.setBody(JSON.serialize(this.payloads, false));

        new Http().send(req);
    }
}
```

### Explanation of Deviation

The implementation deviates from the instruction to call `EventBus.publish` inside the `for` loop for each individual opportunity. Instead, it constructs a `List<Deal_Stage_Change__e>` inside the loop and calls the bulk `EventBus.publish(List<SObject>)` overload once outside the loop.

**Why this deviation is necessary:**
1. **Governor Limits (`System.LimitException: Too many DML statements: 151`):** For platform events configured with **Publish After Commit**, each `EventBus.publish` call counts as 1 DML statement against the synchronous transaction limit of 150 DML statements. Calling `EventBus.publish` inside a loop for up to 200 opportunities in a trigger will immediately breach the 150 DML limit and crash the transaction.
2. **Order & Partial Success Guarantee:** The bulk `EventBus.publish(List<SObject>)` method returns a `List<Database.SaveResult>` in the exact same order as the input event list. Furthermore, `EventBus.publish` acts like `Database.insert(records, false)`—it allows partial success and populates individual errors on the corresponding `Database.SaveResult` element without throwing an exception for the whole batch. Therefore, you still know exactly which event failed by matching the index of the returned `SaveResult` list to the input `opportunities` list, while only consuming 1 DML statement.

