public with sharing class AccountRatingService {
    private static final Decimal HOT_THRESHOLD = 100000;
    private static final String RATING_HOT = 'Hot';
    private static final String RATING_WARM = 'Warm';
    private static final String RATING_COLD = 'Cold';

    /**
     * Single-account overload kept for API convenience.
     */
    public static void recalculate(Id accountId) {
        if (accountId != null) {
            recalculate(new Set<Id>{ accountId });
        }
    }

    /**
     * Bulk entry point. Routes to @future when allowed by the current execution context,
     * or runs synchronously if already inside a future or batch context.
     */
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }
        Set<Id> cleanIds = new Set<Id>(accountIds);
        cleanIds.remove(null);
        if (cleanIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        if (System.isFuture() || System.isBatch()) {
            recalculateNow(cleanIds);
        } else {
            recalculateFuture(cleanIds);
        }
    }

    @future
    public static void recalculateFuture(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        recalculateNow(accountIds);
    }

    public static void recalculateNow(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, String> targetRatingsByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            if (accId != null) {
                targetRatingsByAccount.put(accId, RATING_COLD);
            }
        }

        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT AccountId accId, MAX(Amount) maxAmount, COUNT(Id) openCount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :targetRatingsByAccount.keySet()
              AND IsClosed = false
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            Id accId = (Id) ar.get('accId');
            Integer openCount = (Integer) ar.get('openCount');
            Decimal maxAmount = (Decimal) ar.get('maxAmount');

            if (openCount != null && openCount > 0) {
                if (maxAmount != null && maxAmount >= HOT_THRESHOLD) {
                    targetRatingsByAccount.put(accId, RATING_HOT);
                } else {
                    targetRatingsByAccount.put(accId, RATING_WARM);
                }
            }
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Account acc : [
            SELECT Id, Rating
            FROM Account
            WHERE Id IN :targetRatingsByAccount.keySet()
        ]) {
            String newRating = targetRatingsByAccount.get(acc.Id);
            if (acc.Rating != newRating) {
                acc.Rating = newRating;
                accountsToUpdate.add(acc);
            }
        }

        if (!accountsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update accountsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

### What I Changed and Why

I did **not** call `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(line.Product2Id)` inside the loop as suggested. Here is why and what I did instead:

1. **Avoiding Governor Limit Exceptions (SOQL 101):** `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(Id)` executes a `SELECT` query every time it is called. Because Salesforce enforces a strict limit of 100 SOQL queries per synchronous transaction, calling this method inside a loop for a CPQ quote with up to 200 OpportunityLineItems will immediately fail with a `System.LimitException: Too many SOQL queries: 101`.
2. **Bulkification while keeping rules in one place:** `PricingRules` also exposes `public static Decimal standardDiscountForFamily(String family)`, which contains the actual discount rules without running a query. In `LineItemDiscountHandler`, I bulkified the logic by:
   - Collecting all needed `Product2Id`s (and pulling from `PricebookEntryId` if `Product2Id` wasn't directly populated on the `before insert` record).
   - Executing **a single SOQL query** to fetch the `Family` for all products in the batch.
   - Calling `PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily(product.Family)` in the loop. This keeps `PricingRules` untouched as the single source of truth for discount logic while uses at most 1–2 SOQL queries for the entire 200-line batch.

